<project_instructions>
<file path="$ROOT/HINT.md">
# Root

Root rules apply everywhere.
</file>
<file path="$ROOT/.hint/rules/always.md">
# Always on

Applies to every file.
</file>
<file path="$ROOT/.hint/rules/badglob.md">
# Bad glob

Loads always too.
</file>
<file path="$ROOT/.hint/rules/broken.md">
# Broken header

Still loads, always.
</file>
<file path="$ROOT/.hint/rules/go.md" paths="**/*.go">
# Go

Use gofmt. Keep errors last.
</file>
<file path="$ROOT/sub/AGENTS.md">
Sub rules.
</file>
<file path="$ROOT/sub/.hint/rules/sub.md">
Sub rule, always.
</file>
</project_instructions>
<project_rules>
These rules apply to particular paths and load into the instructions above once a tool reads or writes a matching file; until then only their titles are listed. The instructions tool can read any of them now.
- TypeScript conventions ($ROOT/.cursor/rules/ts.mdc) for *.ts, *.tsx
- deep ($ROOT/sub/.hint/rules/deep.md) for deep/*.go
</project_rules>